From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Addster09 <aadityasingh.cs9@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:28:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] libs: Add MTK GED-KPI support to fix MTK gpufreq Mediatek GPU
 (#25)

scheduler likes to have the timestamps of the frames to be able to adjust
DVFS. Technically this isn't completely needed, because it looks like DVFS
can work once we started triggering /proc/ged. But now that the work is done,
let's do it completely.

In benchmarks on Poco X4 GT, before this patch result is 1500, after is
5700. If we disable the patch after enabling it without rebooting, it
goes to 5400. So looks like GED KPI thingy does try to do a bit more
than just standard DVFS.

Thanks @sarthakroy2002 for the help and support (other people helped as
well) & @claxten10 for enabling it

Guard the code behind a soong flag (@Addster09)

[etnperlong: carried for TB375FC (DerpFest 17), which opts in from its
 device tree with soong_config_set_bool libgui support_mtk_ged_kpi.
 Imported from crDroid 17.0 be7f9ad5297b (crdroidandroid/android_frameworks_native
 PR #25; same change as Evolution-X cc9996b368cc). DerpFest declined to merge
 it and asked for the original author to submit it. Local fixes:
 - Constructor/connect logs: ALOGE -> ALOGD for the one-shot probe result,
   ALOGV for per-surface messages.
 - Zero the probe output so a failed ioctl reads as disabled; disable once
   per process when /proc/ged cannot be opened.
 - "acquire" ioctl: pvParamOut pointed at `in`. GED copies the input before
   the handler and writes the output afterwards, so the kernel was unaffected;
   only `in.pid` was overwritten and `out` stayed zero. Point it at `out`.
 - Check open()/read() of /proc/<pid>/cmdline instead of reading an
   uninitialized buffer on failure.
 The ioctl structures and call sites are unchanged.]

Signed-off-by: Addster09 <aadityasingh.cs9@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Pierre-Hugues Husson <phh@phh.me>
Signed-off-by: Evans Mike <etnperlong@gmail.com>
